{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgdR1bG3YykUGmu89irJP", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The Light at Gallow's Point\n\nFor forty years, Ada Penrose climbed the 112 iron steps each dusk and lit the lamp at Gallow's Point. When her eyesight began to fail, her son Tom offered to take over. She refused, though she couldn't say why.\n\nOne stormy autumn night, the power failed. Ada climbed anyway, her hands finding each rung in the dark, and turned the great brass crank by hand until the beam swept out over the black water.\n\nAt dawn, Tom found her asleep against the lens housing, her palms raw and bleeding.\n\n\"I wanted to see it turn once more,\" she said.\n\nHe didn't argue. Together they walked down the steps, and Tom understood that some duties aren't really about the work. They're about being the one who shows up.\n\nThat evening, he climbed alone, and at dusk the lamp came on, steady and bright, just as she'd always taught him."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 17922, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 2, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "steer-session-1", "uuid": "0f3498df-2616-4d38-b2e6-b06261e5e57b", "timestamp": "2026-11-02T03:46:10.893Z", "request_id": "req_011CgdR1b6skrD7TsJmwtWYf"}
